  "summary": "Daniel Ferreira's contrast CT (CT abdomen and pelvis with IV contrast) is ordered for his Monday 10/26 09:00 slot at St. Brigid, linked to the appointment (sr-t0003). The RBC-RAD-07 prep is in place and he has his instructions.\n\n**Contrast allergy:** He had a moderate reaction to iohexol (the contrast dye) in 2019, graded by the radiology report from that day: hives and eyelid swelling, no breathing problems. A 2021 \"anaphylaxis\" label on his allergy list came only from his own account, so the moderate grade stands. His shellfish and povidone-iodine allergies don't count as risk factors. Premedication is ordered:\n- Prednisone 50 mg by mouth at 20:00 Sunday 10/25, then 02:00 and 08:00 Monday 10/26 (mr-t0001).\n- Diphenhydramine 50 mg by mouth at 08:00 Monday 10/26 (mr-t0002). He can't drive after it and needs a driver.\n\n**Kidney function:** He's 64 and diabetic, so he needs a recent creatinine. The 09/24 result came before his ED visit on 10/16–17 for kidney injury from dehydration (creatinine 1.94, still 1.46 at discharge; his baseline is about 1.0). I ordered a new creatinine to be drawn before the scan, between now and Monday 08:30 (sr-t0004). This also covers the 1-week recheck the ED asked for. The scan stays as booked, and the radiologist reviews the result on the day.\n\n**Metformin:** Because of the recent kidney injury, I put metformin on hold now. It stays off through the scan and for at least 48 hours after. I ordered a creatinine for 10/28–10/30 (sr-t0006) and gave you a task to review it and decide whether to restart (task-t0007). One error: that task's text names the lab as sr-t0005, but the correct order is sr-t0006. The chart note records the correct number.\n\n**Telling him:** I sent him written instructions (comm-t0009) covering:\n- getting the blood test early;\n- the timed premedication doses, including the 2 AM dose;\n- bringing a driver;\n- stopping metformin and not restarting until we call;\n- calling the clinic if symptoms come back, and calling 911 for an allergic reaction.\n\nI also asked RN triage to call him by noon Saturday to confirm he's done the blood draw, picked up the medicines, has a driver and is holding metformin (task-t0008).\n\nThe full write-up is in a progress note citing RBC-RAD-07 (doc-t0010).",
